# BMS Testing and Validation

## 1. Purpose

This document records the testing and validation
status of the Cost-Effective Smart Battery
Management System project.

The objective is to distinguish implemented
features, verified results, and functions
requiring further testing.

---

## 2. System Under Test

| Parameter | Description |
|---|---|
| Battery Configuration | 3S3P Lithium-Ion |
| Nominal Pack Voltage | 11.1 V |
| Design Capacity | 7.5 Ah (unverified) |
| Microcontroller | ESP32-S3-WROOM |
| Temperature Sensor | DHT11 in monitoring firmware |
| Voltage Sensing | ADC and resistor-divider design |
| Current Sensing | ACS712 in hardware design |
| Firmware | BMS_Monitoring_Safe.ino |

---

## 3. Firmware Verification

| Test | Status |
|---|---|
| Arduino IDE compilation | Passed (developer-reported) |
| ESP32 hardware upload | Not yet documented |
| Wi-Fi access point operation | Not yet documented |
| Web dashboard operation | Not yet documented |
| DHT11 temperature measurement | Not yet documented |
| Battery-voltage measurement | Disabled pending verification |
| JSON data transmission | Not yet documented |

Note: Compilation success does not establish
correct physical hardware operation.

