## 5. Testing Evidence

Future test documentation should include:

- Test objective
- Equipment used
- Circuit configuration
- Test procedure
- Reference measurements
- Measured results
- Observations
- Pass/fail criteria

Original prototype photographs and circuit
diagrams are available in the main repository.

---

## 6. Known Limitations

- Battery capacity has not been independently
  verified through a discharge-capacity test.
- The original report contains conflicting
  battery specifications.
- Battery voltage acquisition is disabled
  in the revised monitoring firmware.
- The revised firmware does not implement
  charging control or protective disconnection.
- Hardware validation of the revised firmware
  remains pending.

---

## 7. Safety Notice

This is an educational engineering prototype.

The monitoring firmware is not a certified
Battery Management System and must not be
used as the sole protection mechanism for
a lithium-ion battery.

Live battery fault testing requires appropriate
equipment, protection, and supervision.
